Anaïs Marchal is a late 20s human male, with red hair and dark brown eyes. He's the fraternal twin of [[Anouk Marchal|Anouk]]. Anaïs often wears sharp, plain suits but adorns his fingers and wrists with wooden rings and bracelets. He has a moderately sized raiment of the [[Iridescent Host|Host]].

Anaïs is the more magically-inclined of the twins. His portion of the [[Org/Iconoclasm/index|Iconoclasm]] workshop is dominated by magical tomes and alchemical reagents. He tends to be more reserved than his sister.

Between Anaïs and her sister [[Anouk Marchal|Anouk]], no small amount of hard-won experience stands behind them — seasoned adventurers both, and formidable for it.

He and his sister were born in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]] and raised in [[Geography/Fenrith/index|Fenrith]], and the language they curse in is the one from there. He says he is made of skin, though a hard armoured thing sits behind his head where a skull would be, and he has been 35 for nine months.

Both twins serve [[Divinity/The Narrative/Renge|Renge]] the Fickle Mistress. He has not spoken with her in years; she gives little direction and may grant a great boon or a terrible bane. She cannot be everywhere, so now and then she pulls the twins into a white void to step into an unresolved fight and settle it. Anaïs finds it a little enjoyable to tilt the Scale. He and his sister hold that they are Renge's before any company they keep: if she told them to leave the Party's coalition they would go, though they do not believe she would, and they will promise no more than to stand with its members for now.

He follows leads on the [[Phenomena/Harmony/Voidsong|Voidsong]] and hates [[Aut]], whom he blames for [[Geography/Raelion/index|Raelion]], [[Geography/Brithwyn/index|Brithwyn]] and the Plaguebearer. A convox blip with the Voidsong's harmonics once lured him to a cabin at void 26 in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/index|Sableclutch]], where he was held shackled under Aut's three-dot mark; he believes a friend of Aut's in the church set the lure to catch anyone listening in. He knows of the five narrative siblings, and recognizes [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Pyre|Pyre]], [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Herald|Herald]] and [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Giant|Giant]] among the six gods said to be coming.

He has sworn to kill the Party if they sell the twins out to Aut. He knows about the vaccine the Party carry; his sister does not.
